  "effects": {
    "prepare": "Explicit only: initialize missing owned general registry schema1/current scope generation0. Idempotent for same prepared caller/profile/nativeepisode. When actual native episode or explicit admission profile changes, ordinary read/context/reset/clear refuses context_episode_changed/context_profile_changed; explicit prepare acknowledges the new observed episode/profile and clears ONLY this caller+checkout old-episode cache/events/availability, generation0. Other scopes/data untouched, no archival retention. Native begin/end/identity remain actual hook owner; no fake event or implicit read reset. Foreign/wrong/corrupt existing store refused unchanged.",
    "read": "Source filesystem I/O and decoding/selection occur before acquiring registry guard. Any earlier generation/budget observation is advisory only. After native hook guard where applicable, acquire the same existing general-registry lock used by reset/clear and begin its short transaction. Under this single serialization boundary read final prepared profile/episode/generation, construct the complete FULLCONTENT candidate for that generation, serialize/count chosen representation, and reject over budget BEFORE any read cache/event write. Classify/register the batch and materialize final response from the SAME generation while retaining the guard, then commit and release. Stdout write and source I/O stay outside guards. Reset either completes before that final snapshot (read budgets/registers new generation) or waits until read commits (read returns coherent old generation); no mid-snapshot reset. No new lease/request token/acknowledgement; existing general registry owner provides serialization. All input/source validation failures and final output-limit denial add no read cache/event. Writer follows successful COMMIT as ERP.",
    "reset": "Current project+checkout+caller only; increment current generation once for new event_id, preserve minimum active-episode cache/history needed for classification and statistical facts. Replaying latest identical reset event/reason is idempotent; same event_id/different action or reason is event_conflict. No SessionEnd fabrication or other-scope mutation. Native profile requires the SAME already-prepared observed episode; differentepisode requires explicitprepare first. Every native mutation capturesinitialepisode and finalguard comparesit; lock orderhook->general. Callerprofile cannot silently reuse a context preparedfornativeprofile without explicitprepare. Event replay guarantee is ONLY the latest action of the active preparedscope: same last event_id/operation/reason/profile/episode is idempotent; conflictingreuse of thatlatestID refuses. No indefinite historical ID registry is introduced. Explicit prepare for new observedepisode/profile retires the oldscope action/cache/event data and initializesgeneration0; oldscope IDs are not cross-context identities. Explicit clear retains its ownlatestclear identity so exactreplay remainsidempotent.",
    "clear": "Current project+checkout+caller only; clear reader cache/events/availability, generation0; preserve last clear event identity to make exact replay idempotent. Other scopes and all foreign files untouched. No implicit clear on ordinary read refusal. Same-profile/same-nativeepisode checked; actual scope cannot be selected by payload. Eventreplay identity includesoperation/reason/currentpreparedprofile+episode. No automaticold-episodeclear onreadfallback. Event replay guarantee is ONLY the latest action of the active preparedscope: same last event_id/operation/reason/profile/episode is idempotent; conflictingreuse of thatlatestID refuses. No indefinite historical ID registry is introduced. Explicit prepare for new observedepisode/profile retires the oldscope action/cache/event data and initializesgeneration0; oldscope IDs are not cross-context identities. Explicit clear retains its ownlatestclear identity so exactreplay remainsidempotent.",
    "context": "Read-only current-scope summary and generation, no implicit DB/context creation; cache_entries is active episode total as source snapshot, event aggregates status/classification sorted and total count. Empty/absent current scope requires explicit prepare. Returns context caller_key/generation/admission_mode/native_episode (null for caller mode). Requires explicitprepare on profile/episode mismatch; publicsummary remains readonly.",
    "writer_failure": "Actual sink OSError/BrokenPipeError after registration returns1; stderr has exact typed output_write diagnostic, stdout may be partial. Committed cache/events remain and next equal read may be unchanged. Smallest recovery: inspect actual captured exit/stdout/stderr; explicit scoped reset with new manual event then reread returns content. No ack/delivery-proof/pending states or claim model received text. Return1 is the controlled publicPython sink-failure result. RealCLI broken pipe/final-buffer failure is recorded by the actual runner terminal status/fullstderr; do not fabricate a fixed1/completecapture when Python actually reports another nonzero status. This plan tests the genuine public output port with standardOSError sink, not a fake successful CLI capture.",
    "prepared_lock": "Ordinary read/context/reset/clear requires already prepared ownedregistryDB andownlock; missinggeneralstore/lock is registry_missing, nevercreatedimplicitly. Explicitprepare maypublish/recoveronlyitsvalidatedownedlock aftercheckingcompatibleproject-specificregistryheader; foreign/wrongschema untouched. Nativehook lock isALWAYS existingonly andnevercreatedbyreader."
  },
